    "text": "Finding: Baby-branded videos associated with fewer words at 8 to 16 months (correlational, contested).\nSources: Zimmerman, Christakis & Meltzoff (2007), Associations between media viewing and language development in children under age 2 years, Journal of Pediatrics 151, 364-368. Reanalysis questioning the finding: Ferguson & Donnellan (2014), Developmental Psychology 50, 129-137.\nConfidence: LOW/CONTESTED for harm, which is why the script says 'debated' and leans only on 'did not help.' The 'did not help' point rests on Kuhl 2003 (HIGH) and on the AAP's position that infants do not learn well from video."
