    "text": "Finding: The '30 million word gap' rests on 42 families and did not replicate in a larger multi-community study; the turn-taking findings are the durable part.\nSources: Hart & Risley (1995), Meaningful Differences. Sperry, Sperry & Miller (2019), Reexamining the verbal environments of children from different socioeconomic backgrounds, Child Development 90, 1303-1318. Golinkoff et al. (2019) reply and Sperry et al. (2019) response, Child Development.\nConfidence: HIGH that the specific 30-million figure is contested and the original sample was tiny; MODERATE on 'did not find the gap,' since Golinkoff and colleagues argue directed speech still differs by SES. The script keeps to what both sides accept: turn quality matters more than the slogan."
