    "text": "Finding: When mothers' depression remitted with treatment, their children's symptoms and behavior problems decreased; children of non-remitting mothers did not improve.\nSources: Weissman et al. (2006), Remissions in maternal depression and child psychopathology: a STAR*D-Child report, JAMA, DOI 10.1001/jama.295.12.1389. Pilowsky et al. (2008), American Journal of Psychiatry, DOI 10.1176/appi.ajp.2008.07081286. Wickramaratne et al. (2011), American Journal of Psychiatry, DOI 10.1176/appi.ajp.2010.10010032.\nConfidence: HIGH for the association; observational (mothers were treated, children were not randomized). The children in STAR*D-Child were 7 to 17, not infants, so the script says 'children,' not 'babies.'"
