    "text": "Myth: \"You can tell your baby's attachment style from a quiz or a few behaviors.\"\nWhat the research shows: Researchers warn that attachment classifications are not tools for judging an individual child; even in the lab, coding takes certified coders.\n\nMyth: \"The more sensitive you are, the more secure your baby will be, full stop.\"\nWhat the research shows: Sensitivity is a real cause, shown in experiments, but it explains well under a tenth of the differences between babies. Many other ingredients matter."
