    "text": "Finding: AAP: avoid screen media other than video chatting under 18 months (2016, reaffirmed 2022); 2026 statement: 'Infants under 18 months struggle to transfer information from a screen to the real world.'\nSources: AAP Council on Communications and Media, Hill et al. (2016), Media and Young Minds, Pediatrics, DOI 10.1542/peds.2016-2591; Munzer et al. (2026), Digital Ecosystems, Children, and Adolescents: Policy Statement, Pediatrics, DOI 10.1542/peds.2025-075320.\nConfidence: HIGH for 2016. The 2026 sentence was read 2026-10-03 from a copy of the journal PDF (Pediatrics 157(2), e2025075320).\n\nFinding: Only 24.7% of children under 2 met the zero-screen guideline (63 studies, about 89,000 children).\nSources: McArthur et al. (2022), Global prevalence of meeting screen time guidelines among children 5 years and younger, JAMA Pediatrics, DOI 10.1001/jamapediatrics.2021.6386.\nConfidence: HIGH. Pooled estimate; 'about one in four'."
