    "text": "Finding: Children with consistently high routines across 3 to 5 had fewer attention, externalizing and internalizing problems than those whose routines decreased.\nSources: Selman & Dilworth-Bart (2025), Child Routines Across Preschool and Associations with Socioemotional Adjustment, Journal of Family Psychology, DOI 10.1037/fam0001299 (N = 2,353). Not quoted in the narration; supports 'point the same way'.\nConfidence: MODERATE. Correlational.\n\nFinding: Picture routine and 'what comes next?' prompts.\nSources: Application of contingent scaffolding and routine findings above; not separately tested in this script's sources.\nConfidence: MODERATE. Presented as suggestions, not findings."
