    "text": "Finding: Overjustification: preschoolers who liked drawing with markers and were promised a Good Player award later drew less in free play than unexpected-award and no-award groups.\nSources: Lepper, Greene & Nisbett (1973), Undermining children's intrinsic interest with extrinsic reward, Journal of Personality and Social Psychology, DOI 10.1037/h0035519. Follow-ups: Greene & Lepper (1974), Child Development, DOI 10.1111/j.1467-8624.1974.tb00720.x; Lepper & Greene (1975), DOI 10.1037/h0076484.\nConfidence: HIGH. Classic and replicated. Interest was measured 1 to 2 weeks later; script says 'a week or two later'. 'Special certificate' describes the award."
