    "source": {
      "label": "Growing Minds class, Preschool Years (3 to 5): Lesson 1.4, Behavior at 3, 4, and 5"
    },
    "text": "Between three and five, hitting usually fades, lying and new fears appear, and both are signs of a growing mind. Warm attention, specific praise, and calm, predictable consequences help most.\n\nThat completes Module 1 of this class. Next, we start Module 2, Play as the Work, with pretend play. We'll look at how it changes from three to five, what research can and can't claim about it, and how to join in without taking over.\n\nI'll see you there."
