    "text": "Finding: 96 children tested at 24, 30, 36, 50 and 60 months: inhibitory control at 30 months was strongly related to inhibitory control at 60 months (r = .56).\nSources: Kloo & Sodian (2017), The developmental stability of inhibition from 2 to 5 years, British Journal of Developmental Psychology, DOI 10.1111/bjdp.12197.\nConfidence: MODERATE-HIGH. The same task also showed stable differences between children at 18, 21 and 24 months (Holmboe et al., 2021), so stability is not absent before 30 months. 'Will hold in one moment and fail in the next' is my application about a single child, which these studies do not measure directly."
