    "text": "Finding: Meta-analysis of 35 studies, 16,480 children: household chaos was linked with weaker executive function and effortful control (overall r = .16); in directly tested children, instability (r = .17) mattered more than disorganization (r = .06).\nSources: Andrews et al. (2020/2021), Examining the effects of household chaos on child executive functions: a meta-analysis, Psychological Bulletin, DOI 10.1037/bul0000311.\nConfidence: HIGH that the link exists and is small. The studies cover childhood generally, not only toddlers. Correlational."
