    "text": "Finding: 18 studies of children aged 18 to 60 months with language impairments: parent-implemented interventions had a significant positive effect on receptive and expressive language.\nSources: Roberts & Kaiser (2011), The effectiveness of parent-implemented language interventions: a meta-analysis, American journal of speech-language pathology, DOI 10.1044/1058-0360(2011/10-0055).\nConfidence: HIGH."
