    "text": "Finding: SECOND RESEARCH PASS (v2), slide 13. 49 boys and 41 girls, firstborn, observed at home with the mother on two occasions at 27 months: most interaction involved maternal prohibition of mild misdemeanors, and the children were generally obedient.\nSources: Minton et al. (1971), Maternal control and obedience in the two-year-old, Child Development, DOI 10.2307/1127592.\nConfidence: HIGH for 'generally obedient', which is the abstract's phrase. No percentage is given. An old study (1971) of white firstborn children."
