    "source": {
      "label": "Growing Minds class, Toddler Years (1 to 3): Lesson 4.1, Inside a Tantrum"
    },
    "text": "A tantrum is the alarm at full volume with the brakes still being built. It is not a verdict on your child or on you, and most will fade as the brakes grow.\n\nIn the next lesson, we'll look at the transitions and routines of a toddler's day, where most of the preventable tantrums begin, and I'll see you in that lesson."
